 "text": "The clause is not enforceable as written. Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord cannot require a rent deposit greater than one month's rent. A requirement for two months' rent deposit is therefore unlawful, and the excess is void. Section 7 also voids any term that purports to waive or contract out of the Act's protections.\n\nThe provision that decides the question is section 106, which limits rent deposits to one month's rent and governs how they may be collected and applied. I have not verified the exact current wording of s. 106 against the consolidated statute, so check the e-Laws text before relying on it.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 106",
